WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:18.741
"The parade starts in five minutes!" yelled Katie.

2
00:00:18.742 --> 00:00:21.419
"The wagons are ready!" called Joy.

3
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.924
The twins ran to the front of the parade.

4
00:00:24.925 --> 00:00:29.614
Mr. and Mrs. Pinker sat up high in a covered wagon.

5
00:00:29.615 --> 00:00:33.357
The Pinker children crowded behind them.

6
00:00:33.358 --> 00:00:39.293
"They're traveling just like Howard Lightfoot Jackson and his family!" cried Joy.

7
00:00:39.294 --> 00:00:42.007
"Who?" asked Katie.

8
00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:46.191
"The first family in Willow Creek!" answered Joy.

9
00:00:46.192 --> 00:00:49.118
"Huh?" Katie stared at her twin.

10
00:00:49.119 --> 00:00:51.568
"What do you mean?"

11
00:00:51.569 --> 00:00:58.075
Before Joy could answer, Mr. Pinker shook the reins and his horses started moving.

12
00:00:58.076 --> 00:01:00.392
AJ came running.

13
00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:04.364
"Katie! Ms. Henderson is here!" he yelled.

14
00:01:04.365 --> 00:01:07.352
"She's in the Model T!"

15
00:01:07.353 --> 00:01:09.945
"Who?" asked Joy.

16
00:01:09.946 --> 00:01:14.776
"The oldest person in Willow Creek!" said AJ.

17
00:01:14.777 --> 00:01:19.765
"What?" cried Joy.

18
00:01:19.766 --> 00:01:26.738
"Hello, kids!" Ms. Henderson called. "I've come to the parade!"

19
00:01:26.739 --> 00:01:29.179
"Let's get this car started,"

20
00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:33.137
said Grandpa Henderson, rubbing his hands together.

21
00:01:33.138 --> 00:01:37.245
"First, we pull this and turn that."

22
00:01:37.246 --> 00:01:42.861
Grandpa Henderson jumped out of the car and hurried around to the front.

23
00:01:42.862 --> 00:01:46.570
"Now I turn and pull this handle."

24
00:01:46.571 --> 00:01:50.302
He turned and pulled.

25
00:01:50.303 --> 00:01:54.530
"It started!" everyone shouted.

26
00:01:54.531 --> 00:01:59.223
"It just takes practice," said Grandpa Henderson.

27
00:01:59.224 --> 00:02:03.338
"It's running away!" everyone screamed.

28
00:02:03.339 --> 00:02:07.139
The Model T began rolling toward the street.

29
00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.050
"Get in!" cried Ms. Henderson.

30
00:02:11.051 --> 00:02:15.791
Grandpa Henderson jumped in the car beside his sister.

31
00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:19.728
"Here we go!" he shouted.

32
00:02:19.729 --> 00:02:24.346
"See you at the park!" called the Earthworms.

33
00:02:24.347 --> 00:02:30.037
The high school marching band lined up behind a giant birthday cake.

34
00:02:30.038 --> 00:02:33.838
Then Mrs. Penkov blew her whistle.

35
00:02:33.839 --> 00:02:36.072
"Campers!" she called.

36
00:02:36.073 --> 00:02:39.004
"Get into place behind the band!"

37
00:02:39.005 --> 00:02:42.890
Emily and Carlos unrolled the banner.

38
00:02:42.891 --> 00:02:48.763
"The Willow Creek Day Campers!" read Katie. "That's us!"

39
00:02:48.764 --> 00:02:53.185
The band started playing.

40
00:02:53.186 --> 00:02:55.867
Luke climbed onto his stilts.

41
00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:58.945
"Woo-hoo!" he yelled.

42
00:02:58.946 --> 00:03:03.341
The day campers headed toward Main Street.

43
00:03:03.342 --> 00:03:07.354
As they turned the corner, Joy saw her family.

44
00:03:07.355 --> 00:03:12.945
"Mom, Dad!" she shouted, waving her ribbon twirler.

45
00:03:12.946 --> 00:03:17.930
"Grandpa!" Aunt Sally stood outside Fried Pie Heaven.

46
00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:22.809
"Hello, Aunt Sally!" shouted Katie and Joy.

47
00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:27.989
They turned onto Walnut Street and paraded into the town park.

48
00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:33.651
The band kept playing while everyone ate watermelon and drank lemonade.

49
00:03:33.652 --> 00:03:39.988
Then the mayor made a speech, and the Willow Creek Singers performed old songs.

50
00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:47.001
Finally Mrs. Penkov stepped onto the platform to address the crowd.

51
00:03:47.002 --> 00:03:51.888
"As you know, the day campers had a scavenger hunt this summer."

52
00:03:51.889 --> 00:03:55.126
"Yes, they did. And they were real pests!"

53
00:03:55.127 --> 00:03:57.936
Pete from the post office shouted, laughing.

54
00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:01.344
The crowd laughed too.

55
00:04:01.345 --> 00:04:03.417
Mrs. Penkov continued.

56
00:04:03.418 --> 00:04:06.071
"Now it's time to announce the winners.

57
00:04:06.072 --> 00:04:13.546
Guess what?" The campers held their breath.

58
00:04:13.547 --> 00:04:15.650
"We have a tie!"

59
00:04:15.651 --> 00:04:18.307
The campers gasped.

60
00:04:18.308 --> 00:04:20.586
"Two teams completed their lists.

61
00:04:20.587 --> 00:04:23.758
Both found Willow Creek treasures.

62
00:04:23.759 --> 00:04:32.919
One team found a piece of history—the oldest grave in Willow Creek at the burial place of the first settling family."

63
00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:36.022
Mrs. Penkov unrolled a crayon rubbing.

64
00:04:36.023 --> 00:04:40.162
"Howard Lightfoot Jackson,1848."

65
00:04:40.163 --> 00:04:47.619
"The other team found a living treasure—our oldest citizen," continued Mrs. Penkov.

66
00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:52.422
"Cora Mae Henderson—103 years old.

67
00:04:52.423 --> 00:04:57.128
So the winners are the Tornadoes and the Earthworms!

68
00:04:57.129 --> 00:05:04.796
Each team member wins a ticket for a free day at Big Surf Water Park!" said Mrs. Penkov.

69
00:05:04.797 --> 00:05:09.920
"Big Surf!" cried the Tornadoes and the Earthworms.

70
00:05:09.921 --> 00:05:14.194
"The Double Dip!" cried Joy and Laura.

71
00:05:14.195 --> 00:05:18.804
"The Slippery Spin!" cried Katie and Luke.

72
00:05:18.805 --> 00:05:24.437
The Tornadoes and the Earthworms jumped with joy.

73
00:05:24.438 --> 00:05:31.633
Later that evening, they sat beside the creek and watched fireworks explode in the sky.

74
00:05:31.634 --> 00:05:35.995
"Day camp is over," said Joy with a sigh.

75
00:05:35.996 --> 00:05:41.900
"But we have Willow Creek T-shirts to keep forever," said Laura.

76
00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:46.245
"And we all won the scavenger hunt!" said Luke.

77
00:05:46.246 --> 00:05:51.250
"And we all get to go to Big Surf!" said AJ.

78
00:05:51.251 --> 00:06:02.129
Katie grinned. "Best of all, we still have the rest of the summer to have fun in our Willow Creek!"
